    {
      "_id": "CIIL6R7eRGLt7Dii",
      "name": "Living Vehicle Template",
      "type": "template",
      "img": "icons/svg/item-bag.svg",
      "system": {
        "finalName": "",
        "description": "<p><i>Reference Book: <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Star_Wars_Saga_Edition_Legacy_Era_Campaign_Guide\" title=\"Star Wars Saga Edition Legacy Era Campaign Guide\">Star Wars Saga Edition Legacy Era Campaign Guide</a></i> </p><p><i>See also: <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Yuuzhan_Vong_Biotech\" title=\"Yuuzhan Vong Biotech\">Yuuzhan Vong Biotech</a></i> </p><p>Used to represent everything from Yuuzhan Vong Vehicles to the spacecraft of Zonama Sekot, the&nbsp;Living Vehicle Template&nbsp;allows you to create statistics for biological analogies of existing ships. Though the template won't present the fine mechanical tuning of designing a <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Vehicle\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Vehicle\">Vehicle</a> from scratch, if you just need a basic Living Vehicle comparable in firepower to an X-Wing Starfighter, the Living Vehicle Template should suffice. </p><h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Modifications\">Modifications</span></h3><p>To create a Living Vehicle, make the following changes to an existing Vehicle: </p><table class=\"wikitable\"> \n <tbody>\n  <tr> \n   <th>LIVING VEHICLE SIZE </th> \n   <th> </th> \n   <th>DOVIN BASAL DAMAGE </th>\n  </tr> \n  <tr> \n   <td>Colossal or Smaller </td> \n   <td> </td> \n   <td>7d10x2 </td>\n  </tr> \n  <tr> \n   <td>Colossal (Frigate) </td> \n   <td> </td> \n   <td>5d10x5 </td>\n  </tr> \n  <tr> \n   <td>Colossal (Cruiser) or Larger </td> \n   <td> </td> \n   <td>7d10x5 </td>\n  </tr>\n </tbody>\n</table><ul>\n <li><b><a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Tractor_Beams\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Tractor Beams\">Tractor Beams</a>:</b> <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Yuuzhan_Vong_Vehicles\" title=\"Yuuzhan Vong Vehicles\">Yuuzhan Vong Vehicles</a> can use their Dovin Basals as <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Tractor_Beams\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Tractor Beams\">Tractor Beams</a>. Other kinds of Living Vehicles have comparable alternatives to emulate a Tractor Beam's effects.</li> \n <li><b><a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Weapon_Systems\" title=\"Weapon Systems\">Weapon Systems</a>:</b> Living Vehicles have analogues for most <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Weapon_Systems\" title=\"Weapon Systems\">Weapon Systems</a>. <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Weapon_Systems\" title=\"Weapon Systems\">Weapon Systems</a> that deal Energy damage alone typically deal <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Fire\" title=\"Fire\">Fire</a> damage instead of normal Energy damage. Other <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Weapon_Systems\" title=\"Weapon Systems\">Weapon Systems</a>, even <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Ion\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Ion\">Ion</a> weapons, have analogues on a Living Vehicle. They behave exactly as the <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Weapon_System\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Weapon System\">Weapon System</a> does on the base <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Vehicle\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Vehicle\">Vehicle</a>.</li>\n</ul>",
